NAME
    useradd - create a user account (root only)

SYNOPSIS
    useradd <name> [-u <uid>] [-g <group|gid>]

DESCRIPTION
    Adds an account to /etc/passwd and prompts (twice, no echo) for its initial
    password. ROOT ONLY. Creates the home directory /User/<name> and, on ext2,
    chowns it to the new user.

    -u <uid>          use this uid (default: the next free id at/above 1000)
    -g <group|gid>    primary group by name or number (default: a user-private
                      group named after the user, created in /etc/group with
                      gid == uid, the usual convention)

    The password salt is derived from the monotonic clock (there is no hardware
    RNG yet), so it is weak but per-account unique. Account files hold ~20
    entries (a 2 KB read cap).

EXAMPLES
    # useradd alice
    New password: ****
    Retype new password: ****
    useradd: created alice

    # groupadd devs
    # useradd bob -g devs        put bob in the existing group "devs"

SEE ALSO
    passwd, usermod, groupadd, id, su, login
